{"ts":"2026-08-29T23:37:03.326Z","seq":80,"src":"server","type":"note","stage":"Penciler","execution":"56b3e06c","message":"Pass 4. The multiply overlay of pass 3 put both eye clusters, both crania, the right chest edge, the crown and jaw chains and the trunk edges on the reference. One mass was still wrong: the far ear at rx46 reached x97 where the reference reaches x110, so it is widened to rx52 c(58,134) — chord 109.5 against a measured 110. Right-ear positions LOOK 5px left in the overlay but the row scans give 397-445 and 459-525 at y=0 across three rows, so I am trusting the measurement over my eye and recording the discrepancy rather than nudging to taste."}
